tps://senzing.com/request-non-prod-license/. These three options belong to that imminent load only — do NOT raise them while installing, configuring, or merely explaining Senzing, and never on a host where Senzing is not installed: there is no load there to take a sample of. Even with a license, this single-threaded environment is not recommended for more than 10,000 records — for larger datasets, guide them to a dedicated loading pipeline."],"install_commands":["# Prerequisite — the sqlite3 CLI (package name: sqlite). In a container you are root: run every command below WITHOUT sudo.","sudo yum install -y sqlite","# SQLite version: Senzing documents >= 3.38 for v4; the engine refuses to start below 3.35.0 ("Minimum required version is 3.35.0"), so stock RHEL 9 (3.34.1) and RHEL 8 fail at startup. Run: sqlite3 --version. If older: build SQLite (e.g. 3.50.x) from source into /usr/local, then echo /usr/local/lib | sudo tee /etc/ld.so.conf.d/sqlite-local.conf && sudo ldconfig (verified on EL9) — or use PostgreSQL — before creating the database below.","# Install the senzingrepo package to configure the correct yum source for your OS","sudo yum install https://senzing-production-yum.s3.amazonaws.com/senzingrepo-2.0.2-1.noarch.rpm","# EULA acceptance — BEFORE running this command, ASK the user: 'Installing Senzing requires accepting the Senzing End User License Agreement. Do you accept the EULA? (see senzing.com/end-user-license-agreement/)' Only proceed if they confirm.","export SENZING_ACCEPT_EULA=I_ACCEPT_THE_SENZING_EULA","# Minimal SDK install (runtime + setup) — sufficient for SDK-only workflows","sudo yum install -y senzingsdk-runtime senzingsdk-setup","# If you cannot run yum install (containers, CI, no sudo), extract the packages directly instead:","#   rpm2cpio senzingsdk-runtime-*.rpm | cpio -idmv && rpm2cpio senzingsdk-setup-*.rpm | cpio -idmv","#   Then set CONFIGPATH, RESOURCEPATH, SUPPORTPATH, PYTHONPATH, and LD_LIBRARY_PATH to point into your extraction directory."],"name":"Linux (RHEL/Fedora/Amazon Linux)","post_install":["# Verify installation","ls /opt/senzing/er/lib/libSz.so","# Create SQLite database directory (the DB file is NOT auto-created)","mkdir -p /tmp/sqlite","# Create the SQLite database schema (required for senzingsdk-setup; senzingsdk-poc's sz_create_project does this automatically)","sqlite3 /tmp/sqlite/G2C.db < /opt/senzing/er/resources/schema/szcore-schema-sqlite-create.sql"],"prerequisites":["The sqlite3 CLI (package name: sqlite) — post_install uses it to create the SQLite schema. Minimal images may not ship it; the first install command installs it.","SQLite version (only if you use SQLite): Senzing documents SQLite >= 3.38 for v4 (quickstart and airgapped install: "Senzing v4 requires SQLite >= v3.38"), and the engine itself refuses to start below 3.35.0, failing with "Minimum required version is 3.35.0" — so stock RHEL 9 (SQLite 3.34.1) and RHEL 8 fail at engine startup, and Senzing notes no pre-built >= 3.38 package exists for them. Check first: sqlite3 --version. Remedy verified on EL9: build SQLite >= 3.38 (e.g. 3.50.x, https://www.sqlite.org/download.html — needs gcc and make) from source into /usr/local (./configure --prefix=/usr/local && make && sudo make install), then register it with the dynamic linker: echo /usr/local/lib | sudo tee /etc/ld.so.conf.d/sqlite-local.conf && sudo ldconfig (confirm: ldconfig -p | grep libsqlite3). Or use PostgreSQL.","Inside a container you are already root and sudo is NOT installed: run every command below WITHOUT sudo."]}},"next_action":"NEXT CALL: sdk_guide(topic='configure', platform='linux_yum') — Configure the engine and register data sources.","next_steps":[{"description":"Configure the engine and register data sources","params":{"language":null,"platform":"linux_yum","topic":"configure"},"tool":"sdk_guide"}],"topic":"install"}

