{"anti_patterns":[{"category":"platform","correct":"Not applicable — setupEnv is POC-only, does not set SENZING_ENGINE_CONFIGURATION_JSON","pattern":"source setupEnv in SDK code","severity":"error","topics":["install","configure","full_pipeline"]},{"category":"ecosystem","correct":"Build your own images from senzing/senzingsdk-runtime base — pre-built images are for evaluation only, no SLA on security patches","pattern":"Pre-built Docker Hub images in production","severity":"warning","topics":["install","full_pipeline"]},{"category":"ecosystem","correct":"Use official senzing/ organization repos — senzing-garage contains experimental/internal/legacy code that may be unsupported or broken","pattern":"Using senzing-garage repos","severity":"warning","topics":["install","full_pipeline"]}],"compatibility_notes":["CHOOSING linux_yum vs linux_apt: read /etc/os-release on the TARGET host (ID / ID_LIKE) — rhel, centos, rocky, almalinux, ol, fedora or amzn -> linux_yum (.rpm); debian or ubuntu -> linux_apt (.deb). `uname` does not show the distribution.","DEPENDENCY: The Rust SDK (sz-rust-sdk) is NOT on crates.io. You MUST use a git dependency. Add to Cargo.toml: sz-rust-sdk = { git = "https://github.com/brianmacy/sz-rust-sdk" }. Do NOT invent a version number."],"eval_license":{"message":"Need a Senzing license to try this? Open Ask Senzing — the assistant pop-up on https://docs.senzing.com — and just ask it for a free evaluation license; it will give you one.","url":"https://docs.senzing.com"},"install":{"direct_download":{"description":"Direct download alternative for firewalled environments — no package-repository configuration needed. Follow `install_steps` in order: the Senzing EULA is accepted FIRST, then each package's `fetch` command downloads it from its `url` (served by this MCP server) and it is installed. These packages cover more than one CPU architecture (aarch64, x86_64). Run `uname -m` on the target host and use ONLY the packages whose `arch` equals its output.","install_steps":["[aarch64] EULA FIRST — before running ANY command below, show the user the Senzing End User License Agreement (https://senzing.com/end-user-license-agreement/) and ask: 'Installing Senzing requires accepting the Senzing EULA. Do you accept it?' Continue only on an explicit yes; the acceptance variable in the install command below is that answer.","[aarch64] Host prerequisites (the install cannot fetch them offline): libc6 >= 2.34 and libssl3 — these bundled packages are for Ubuntu 22.04 / Debian 12 or newer; for older releases use the Senzing apt repository's build for that release (install_commands, or carry it in) — plus less (required by senzingsdk-tools). `dpkg -s` only shows they are installed, not new enough. Check against the packages' real requirements, offline, before installing: sudo apt-get install --simulate ./senzingsdk-runtime_4.4.2-26272_arm64.deb ./senzingsdk-setup_4.4.2-26272_arm64.deb ./senzingsdk-tools_4.4.2-26272_arm64.deb   It must print an Inst line per package and no "Depends: … but it is not installable" errors.","[aarch64] Run each package's `fetch` command (listed in `packages`; it downloads `url` into the current directory), then check its sha256. On Windows PowerShell write `curl.exe` instead of `curl`.","[aarch64] Authenticity: the .deb files carry NO per-package signature (Senzing's apt repository signs its Release index instead), and apt performs no signature check when it installs a local ./file.deb — there is no signature step to run, so do not invent one. Their authenticity rests on each package's `sha256`, which this server checked against the SHA256 that Senzing's apt repository index publishes when it bundled them. Compare before installing: sha256sum ./senzingsdk-runtime_4.4.2-26272_arm64.deb ./senzingsdk-setup_4.4.2-26272_arm64.deb ./senzingsdk-tools_4.4.2-26272_arm64.deb","[aarch64] Install all packages in ONE command, in this order (runtime → setup → tools): sudo env SENZING_ACCEPT_EULA=I_ACCEPT_THE_SEN