The JAR verification warning occurs when the native libraries are not in the standard Senzing install directory (e.g., /opt/senzing/er/lib). This is cosmetic — everything works fine. The check cannot currently be disabled. If using a Nexus/Artifactory that renames JARs (e.g., sz-sdk-4.1.0.jar), the warning is expected and harmless.

Keywords: sz-sdk.jar, Maven, Java, JAR warning, native libraries","relevance_score":164.337158203125,"section":"FAQ","source_url":"https://www.senzing.com/docs/java/4","title":"Where is sz-sdk.jar on Maven Central? I get WARNING Unable to find the sz-sdk.jar","version":"4"},{"category":"sdk","excerpt":"The **`mvn install:install-file`** command can be used to install a jar file in your local repository. To simplify this, version 4.1.0 (or newer) of **`sz-sdk.jar`** doubles as an executable jar file and you can use **`java -jar sz-sdk.jar`** to generate the Apache Maven command to achieve this on your system.

USAGE: java -jar sz-sdk.jar [options]

Options:
